The first one refers to the Count of the ArrayList. In an ArrayList, the count is incremented whenever an element is inserted (`Add` method being called). It implies that the count is indeed being maintained properly.
The second comment refers to the index of the inserted `item` into ArrayList, and the `IndexOf` function. It is true only when the `item` is present in the list and returns more than 0.
The third one refers to the insert operation, where it verifies if the element was successfully inserted at the index by checking if the element at provided index equals the newly inserted value (`_items[index] == value`), and the count increased by one (`_size == OLD(_size) + 1`).
Finally, the fourth comment refers to the LastIndexOf function, which basically returns the index of last occurrence of the item, it is also true when the item is present in the list and its index is more than 0. 
Note: The comments need to be read as part of the code and the debug assertion will hold true. However, it wouldn't trigger a breakpoint as it would be inside an array, a property, or a method, not a standalone entity.--------------------